      "content": "Liquefaction and seismic vulnerability are not minor technicalities; they represent catastrophic failure modes that undermine the absolute safety of the entire building. Even if the risk seems localized to \"minor\" events, the cumulative effect of soil instability over 50-100 years makes the structure fundamentally unreliable for public use. Rejection is justified because no significant economic benefit can ethically outweigh the legal and moral liability of potentially sinking or collapsing thousands of lives without adequate, expensive mitigation.",
