      "content": "I get the safety concern, but I feel like we might be overreacting to the worst-case scenario. Horizon Build mentioned they'd be using advanced deep-foundation pile driving to bypass those soft layers anyway. If we can just frame the liquefaction risk as something that's \"manageable through modern engineering standards\" rather than a \"catastrophic failure,\" it would satisfy the safety boards without killing the development. Don't you think it's more productive to look at how we can approve this with specific safety stipulations, rather than just flat out saying no?",
